## Shared visual grammar

- Primary background `#07060b`, surfaces `#13101d` and `#1b172a`, foreground `#f7f4ec`.
- Accent hierarchy: pink `#ff007a` (creative focus and selected nav), cyan `#00d4ff` (navigation, trace, evidence), yellow `#ffd400` (editorial/emphasis), violet `#9d4edd` (research/secondary category), green `#00e676` (only verified positive statuses).
- Distressed ink/grit/sticker treatment stays behind text; treat noise as decoration, never as replacement for spacing or contrast.
- One navigation shell and typography hierarchy across all screenshots; each work surface has a different information architecture.
- Massive italic display headings; readable editorial body text, monospace for IDs, intentional colored badges with textual labels.
- Different evidence modes must remain distinct: source, interpretation, witness, research proposal, fictional universe, and reviewed publication.
- Respect `id`/`en`, keyboard/focus, reduced motion, privacy, rights and semantically meaningful loading/error/empty states in actual implementation.
- Public Dock, creative SHADOW, scholarly MoonLab, private Harbor, commercial WORKS, bounded SKYLINK require different interaction semantics even when they share tokens.
- The graphic references do not supersede accepted ADRs or verify TODO completion.

## Implementation order

Preserve existing ARSY Hub and SIGNAL/RADIO runtime; reuse `@moonwitness/moonui`; build reusable shell, cards, evidence badges, data tables, creative canvases, provenance inspectors and state-led controls. Implement each page only under corresponding TODO evidence gates. Avoid new branches; project policy develops on `dev` and promotes verified changes to `main`.

## Distribution

12 distinct PNGs plus this guide and the contact sheet. No font files are distributed.